This is a statement of a philosophical position which by its own criteria
is meaningless. 

To say that  "existence exists" is non-operational may be accurate. To say
that it is stupid, or wrong, or a waste of time may give us some
information. But to say that it's meaningless exhibits incredible gall (an
extropian virtue?) and mammoth myopia (an extropian virtue - not). 

Unlike philosophers, who can safely spend their entire lives innocent of
any but the most naive notions of 'hard science,' 'hard scientists' have to
live in a human world  of meaning. Trying to redefine meaning to please
one's self will not do the trick.

